{"id": "EUVD-2026-80996", "enisaUuid": "bf19e1e8-6598-3e6f-8d96-c1f36961b1f2", "description": "On affected platforms running Arista EOS with VRRPv2 IP-AH authentication configured, an unauthenticated attacker within the same layer 2 network segment on which VRRP is running can capture a legitimate authenticated VRRP advertisement and replay it indefinitely. Replayed advertisements can be used to advertise stale VRRP state, for example to prevent a backup router from taking over the virtual gateway after the original master has gone down, resulting in a denial of service for hosts using the virtual gateway address.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T18:47:30", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-17T18:33:52", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:A/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://www.arista.com/en/support/advisories-notices/security-advisory/24713-security-advisory-0157"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-73443", "GHSA-vq3p-3r98-j8w8"], "assigner": "Arista", "epss": 0.27, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "66ef5df2-e1aa-3246-a93d-a655bce2d96b", "product": {"name": "EOS", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "4.35.0 \u22644.35.5M"}, {"id": "78674560-0ba3-30e8-adcf-a8ea4df564e0", "product": {"name": "EOS", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "4.34.0 \u22644.34.7M"}, {"id": "e90bb32b-80b5-32b1-b3f8-fbd840396583", "product": {"name": "EOS", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "4.36.0 \u22644.36.1F"}, {"id": "f8535801-bd0f-3b0b-89b2-df0fc7a136ff", "product": {"name": "EOS", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}, "product_version": "4.33.0 \u22644.33.9M"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "4a4602f1-9105-3a20-ba11-4e5e087c9a9c", "vendor": {"name": "Arista Networks"}}], "isExploited": false}